<div class="bhd-page__keypoints" aria-label="Research partnership standards"><div><strong>Question first</strong><span>Start with a defined hydration problem or hypothesis, not a desired marketing conclusion.</span></div><div><strong>Method matters</strong><span>Endpoints, comparison conditions, population and analysis should match the question being asked.</span></div><div><strong>Status stays visible</strong><span>Planned, underway, completed and published work should never be presented as the same thing.</span></div></div>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid"><article class="bhd-page__prose"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Why collaborate</p><h2>Better evidence requires more than product access</h2><p>Hydration research can involve physiology, behaviour, performance, clinical context, implementation and product formulation. The right collaborator helps define which of those questions is actually being studied and which methods can answer it.</p><p>Best Hydrate is interested in collaborations that can improve understanding even when the result is narrower or less commercially convenient than expected. That is more valuable than a study designed only to generate a favourable sentence for advertising.</p></article><aside class="bhd-page__callout"><span class="bhd-page__callout-label">Research standard</span><h3>Research is not pre-written marketing.</h3><p>The question, protocol and interpretation should be strong enough to remain useful regardless of the direction of the result.</p></aside></section>

<section class="bhd-page__split"><div class="bhd-page__split-media"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/8533097/pexels-photo-8533097.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1500" alt="Researchers reviewing documents and laboratory samples together" width="1500" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="bhd-page__split-copy"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Ways to work together</p><h2>From exploratory pilots to publication-ready studies</h2><ul><li>Study-question and protocol development</li><li>Product or formulation evaluation under defined conditions</li><li>Hydration, urinary, performance or implementation endpoints</li><li>Student projects and pilot studies with appropriate supervision</li><li>Grant-supported collaborative research</li><li>Knowledge translation after results are complete</li></ul><p>The appropriate model depends on the question, institution, ethics requirements and available resources.</p></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Governance expectations</p><h2>Four principles before data collection begins</h2><div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--4"><article><h3>Roles</h3><p>Define sponsor, investigator, analyst and operational responsibilities clearly.</p></article><article><h3>Ethics</h3><p>Human-participant work should follow the applicable institutional and regulatory review requirements.</p></article><article><h3>Conflicts</h3><p>Funding, product support and company involvement should be disclosed appropriately.</p></article><article><h3>Publication</h3><p>Agree early on how results, including unfavourable results, can be reported or published.</p></article></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__feature"><div><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Current evidence program</p><h2>See what is already public before proposing the next study</h2><p>The Science section separates publications, current research, collaborators, impact pathways and clinical development so prospective research partners can see what is established and where questions remain open.</p><a class="bhd-page__button" href="/pages/current-research">Review Current Research</a></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__brand-context"><div><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Research inquiry</p><h2>Bring a question, not just a collaboration label</h2><p>Tell us the population, research question, proposed methods, institution or team, and what role you think Best Hydrate could reasonably play.</p></div><div class="bhd-page__brand-actions"><a class="bhd-page__button" href="/pages/contact">Contact Us</a><a class="bhd-page__button bhd-page__button--secondary" href="/pages/research-partners">Current Research Partners</a></div></section>

